6. Important Technical Decisions
Client-Side Data Persistence (Fast & Offline-First):

Decision: Used local browser storage / lightweight database for initial data persistence.

Reason: Allows the app to work offline instantly without setup friction or expensive cloud server overhead during early testing.

Component-Based Modular Structure:

Decision: Separated UI components (Book Cards, Shelf Lists, Search Bar) into independent modules.

Reason: Keeps code clean, readable, and easy to scale when adding new features later.

Simple, Minimalist UI Design:

Decision: Focused on raw utility and clean spacing over complex, heavy graphic frameworks.

Reason: Ensures fast page loads and seamless navigation across desktop and mobile devices.

⚠️ 7. Known Issues & Future Plans
Known Issues
No Authentication Yet: Currently, data is tied to the local session/device; user accounts are not yet enabled.

Manual Metadata Input: Automatic cover image and metadata fetching via open APIs (e.g., Google Books API) is currently basic and may require manual entry for lesser-known books.

